1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Singapore's Cyber Resilience Mandate: What It Means for Your Archive. A guide for Singapore compliance and IT teams

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:17,655
On 22 July 2026, Singapore's Cyber Security Agency (CSA) said boards of critical infrastructure (CII) operators must own cyber recovery, not just prevention.

3
00:00:17,655 --> 00:00:22,844
Each board must keep a documented cyber resilience framework, reviewed at least annually.

4
00:00:22,844 --> 00:00:28,500
The gap most document archives have is recovery: what happens, in writing, when attackers get in.

5
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:38,515
Risk tolerance: thresholds the board has agreed. Mitigation: measures that reduce the risk. Transfer: mechanisms such as insurance and contractual indemnities.

6
00:00:38,515 --> 00:00:47,758
Recovery: a plan, reviewed annually and signed off at board level. CII operators must also work toward Cyber Trust Mark Level 5, covering 22 cybersecurity domains.

7
00:00:47,758 --> 00:00:51,500
Applies across all 11 critical sectors under the Cybersecurity Act

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:03,500
Who: Auditors and service providers to CII operators. Deadline: 31 December 2026. Who: CII operators and their non-CII-supporting systems. Deadline: 31 December 2027.

9
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,941
Many document strategies are strong on prevention: encryption, access control and firewalls.

10
00:01:09,941 --> 00:01:15,559
They are weaker on recovery once digital records are compromised, encrypted or quietly altered.

11
00:01:15,559 --> 00:01:21,296
A cloud backup encrypted alongside the primary system is a second copy of the same vulnerability.

12
00:01:21,296 --> 00:01:26,500
An LE500 microfilm roll is physically air-gapped: it has no network interface to attack.

13
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:33,845
1. Identify board-critical records: statutory filings, contracts, ledgers, personnel records, drawings. 2.

14
00:01:33,845 --> 00:01:38,933
Keep existing digital backups: microfilm sits alongside them, not instead of them. 3.

15
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:44,500
Write a permanent copy to microfilm: the AW3 COM system writes digital records to LE500 film.

16
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:56,297
Does this replace MAS TRM or PDPA duties? No. It layers on top, adding board-level documented ownership of recovery. Does it matter if we are not classed as CII? Yes.

17
00:01:56,297 --> 00:02:03,126
The ransomware exposure is the same, without a deadline forcing action. How does microfilm help recovery?

18
00:02:03,126 --> 00:02:09,500
It cannot be encrypted, deleted or altered over a network, so it is a demonstrable recovery asset.

19
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,209
